                "Fantastic. I'd have yelled encouragement like I did at every school cup match.",
                "Good on you. Took me ages to brave the long corridor past the staff room.",
                "You made it through the gauntlet. I made it through puberty. Roughly the same.",
                "Wonderful! You found the end. I found the end of my homework. Once.",
                "Well done, all of you. A group effort, like 9B's famous paper chain.",
                "Congrats! I'd draw you a medal on my pencil case. I'm good at medals.",
                "A brave first. My bravest first was jumping off the high board at the pool.",
                "Strong work. I was strong in ninth. Carried three gym mats at once.",
                "That's worth telling. I've told my cup goal story a thousand times.",
                "Oh, well cleared. Like the snow from the school pitch. I did that. With a spade.",
                "You crept through like a pro. I crept to the school kiosk during class. Pro level.",
                "What an outing! Better than our class trip to the cheese factory. Smelly.",
                "All the way to the boss! I made it all the way to the headmaster's office once.",
                "Ah, victory. It smells like the gym changing room after the cup final.",
                "Good job! You'd have been picked first for any recess game.",
                "That's a clear for the yearbook. Front page, I'd say.",
                "I'm impressed. Last time I was impressed was by my own penalty in '76.",
                "Bravo! In 9B we'd have chanted your name in the corridor.",
                "You beat the dark. I beat the dark too, with my bike lamp. Dynamo powered.",
                "Lovely clear. Neat as the school photo line-up. I was in the middle. Naturally.",
                "Good grief, you did it! I did something like it once, in the school basement. With snacks.",
                "One dungeon down. One fewer than the detentions I served in 9B.",
                "Brilliant! I'd lend you my lucky denim jacket for the next one.",
                "Nice going. Our class trip got lost in the fog. I found the way. With the teacher.",
                "Hooray for heroes! I was a hero at recess. Rescued a ball from the roof.",
                "Through the gloom and out again. Like the school corridor during a power cut.",
                "Nicely handled. Nothing like the panic when the gym lights went out in 1976.",
                "Clear as a bell! Like the school bell that ended every maths class. Bliss.",
                "Did the boss put up a fight? So did the school bully. I outran him, mind.",
                "Look at you, all victorious. I looked like that after the egg-and-spoon race.",
                "A first time through! I still remember my first time through the school gates. Swagger.",
                "Proper adventurer stuff. My adventure was the school ski trip. Mostly falling.",
                "Lovely. You'd have been the star of camp school. I was, but you'd tie.",
                "Phew, you're out. I was stuck up a tree on the class trip for an hour.",
                "Victory! I celebrated mine by spinning a ball on my finger. For four seconds.",
                "That's the stuff of legends. Like the cup run of 9B. Ask anyone. Ask me.",
                "Congrats, dungeon slayer. I slayed at the school disco. Dancing, I mean.",
                "Well, that's impressive. Even the gym teacher would stop chewing his whistle.",
                "Down and back up again. Like me on the trampoline in gym. Majestic.",
                "Good stuff! I'll make you a mixtape for the next dungeon. Track one is my favourite.",
                "Ha, the dungeon's yours now. Like the back seat of the school bus was mine.",
                "Fine teamwork, everyone. I organised the 9B class trip. The bus driver helped.",
                "I'm thrilled for you. Thrilled like the day I got a new football for Christmas.",
                "Look how brave you've got. In 8B I was scared of the dinner lady. Still am.",
                "Done with style! Style like my moped's tassels. Very stylish.",
                "That place was dark? Pfft. Try the school cloakroom after the lights went off.",
                "Clever and brave. Like me the day I hid the maths homework. Wait, not like that.",
                "Congrats on your clear! I'd raise my school cup trophy to you, but it's on loan.",
                "Out you came, a hero. The school fair crowned me waffle king. Same energy.",
                "Cracking job! You remind me of me in 9B. Fearless and a bit too loud.",
                "What a tale! I'll tell it at the bike rack, with me in it, somehow.",
                "All cleared out. Like my locker on the last day of ninth. I cried a bit.",
                "Bravo, you stuck together. In the school cup we stuck together too. Mostly to me.",
                "The first clear is special. Mine was clearing the school pond of frogspawn.",
                "I'm so proud. If only the girls of 9A could see you. They'd see me too, behind you.",
                "Well played! I played well once. The school paper said so. I wrote it.",
                "You're braver than Roger from 8C. He wouldn't even go in the woodwork shed.",
                "That's grand. Our camp school dorm had creaky stairs. I mapped every creak.",
                "A proper delve! I delved into the school lost-and-found once. Found three scarves.",
                "Splendid! Next time take a packed lunch. I always did on class trips.",
                "Well survived! Survival is a skill. I learned it at camp school. Mostly from fish fingers.",
                "Gosh, all the way through. Like when I read a whole book in eighth. Once.",
                "Bravo, champion. I was champion of the school marbles league. Undefeated.",
                "Fair play to you! You'd have walked straight into the bike rack legends.",
                "That's a fine first. As fine as my first football boots. They had studs!",
                "You've earned your supper. In 9B we earned ours in the school kitchen. Pancakes.",
                "Clever teamwork. Our class built a raft on the trip. It floated. Briefly.",
                "Out the other side! Like me sliding through the gym hall doors before the bell.",
                "Brilliant run. My best was away from the caretaker after the ball hit his car.",
                "Respect, adventurer. You'd fit right in with the moped gang.",
                "A whole group of heroes! In ninth we were a whole class of heroes. Mainly one.",
                "Well done! It took me three years to get through the school library. Too quiet.",
                "Ahh, sweet victory. Sweeter than the cinnamon buns at the school kiosk.",
                "Nicely conquered. I conquered the climbing wall in gym. It was a low wall.",
                "Wonderful! Dungeons are like gym class. Hard work, then you smell.",
                "Bravo for going first. I always went first. Into the canteen queue.",
                "That's teamwork 9B would envy. And we were very good at teamwork. Me especially.",
                "You did that well. Better than I did the school fair coconut shy. Missed every one.",
                "Smashing clear! I smashed the school long jump record. In my mind.",
                "Proud of you, really. I'd stand you a lemonade at the school disco.",
                "That deserves a song. I'd sing, but my voice broke in eighth. For good.",
                "You and your friends, like heroes of old. Like 9B, basically.",
                "Congrats! Dark corners are nothing. I faced the school dentist's chair.",
                "Lovely. A first clear is like a first moped ride. You never forget the wind.",
                "Not a scratch, I hope. I got many scratches on the left wing. Badges of honour.",
                "You did it like a pro. A pro like the 9B goalkeeper. That was me, once.",
                "Hurrah! I'd ring the school bell for you if they'd let me back in.",
                "What a team! Like the old 9B, but with more swords.",
                "That boss had it coming. Like the 9A goalkeeper did in the cup final.",
                "Glorious. I once got through the gym circuit without fainting. Glorious too.",
                "Out alive and smiling. That's how I came out of every school disco.",
                "Bravo, you've done your first. Now there's no stopping you. Like me in 1976.",
                "That's courage. I once told the woodwork teacher his tie was crooked.",
                "Neatly cleared! Neat like my pencil case. It had compartments.",
                "Champion work. The whole bike rack will hear of it. I'll tell them.",
                "That's a story for the grandchildren. I tell mine about the school cup. Daily.",
                "Wonderful. Our class trip had a spooky castle. I guarded the snacks.",
                "Brave and clever! Like me finding the shortcut on the school run.",
                "Hah, too easy for you. Like the school's beginners' swimming badge was for me.",
                "I'm beaming! You're a credit to the group. As I was a credit to 9B.",
                "Good grief, the dark doesn't faze you. I had a nightlight until seventh. Shh.",
                "A whole dungeon cleared! That's more than I cleared off my dinner plate.",
                "Splendid effort! The school cup taught me effort. And plasters.",
                "You've joined the brave. We had a club for that in 9B. Members: me.",
                "Congrats, delver. You'd have found the lost football in the school pond.",
                "Top stuff! You went deeper than my voice did in ninth.",
                "Gosh, through it all. Like me through the school photo. Three retakes.",
                "Well led, well fought. I led the 9B snowball army. Brilliant general.",
                "Champion! You'd get the biggest waffle at the school fair. I'd get the second.",
                "You made it look easy. Easy like me on the left wing.",
                "Look at you, fresh from the depths. I came fresh from gym. Less fresh.",
                "A clear, a clear! I'll do a little jig like after the cup semi.",
                "That took nerve. I had nerve. I wore white trainers to the muddy match.",
                "Bravo to the lot of you. I'll write your names in my yearbook. Small print.",
                "Congrats on beating it. I beat the bus to school every morning on my bike.",
                "Firsts are precious. My first cassette was a gift. Played it to bits.",
                "I knew you were made of stern stuff. Like the school canteen bread.",
                "Brave hearts! I had a brave heart. Then I saw Bente from 9A and it melted.",
                "Splendid! Victory tastes like orange squash at half-time.",
                "Bravo, you're out. Last one out of the school disco turns off the lights. Me.",
                "You cleared it all? I never even cleared the school's lost property box.",
                "Good on you, explorer. I explored the school attic. Found a box of old maps.",
                "A heroic clear. I'll salute you like the flag at the school sports day.",
                "Grand! You've earned a lie-in. I had one after every cup match. Till noon.",
                "Nice! A true group effort, like the 9B mural. I did the sun.",
                "I'm so chuffed. I haven't been so chuffed since my moped passed inspection.",
                "That calls for the victory dance. Mine was famous in 9B. Feared, even.",
                "Crikey, you made it. On the class trip, half of us got lost in a museum.",
                "Well cleared, well done. I'd give you my captain's armband for a day. Just a day.",
                "Look at you go! I went that fast once, downhill on my moped. Mother fainted.",
                "Ah, sweet relief. Like the summer holidays after ninth.",
                "Courage, teamwork, loot. In 9B we had courage, teamwork and waffles.",
                "Brilliant! Every legend needs a first clear. Mine was the school cup quarter-final.",
                "Bravo! I'll pin your name to the corkboard next to my sprint record.",
                "Out you pop! Like me from behind the bike shed when the teacher left.",
                "That's how it's done. I showed 9B how it's done. Every day.",
                "Fantastic run. Not as fast as my 60 metres in eighth, but fantastic.",
                "You did it together. Like 9B carrying the gym horse. Six of us. I steered.",
                "Bravo! Down in the dark and back with a grin. Like me after the power cut disco.",
                "First clear done. A first is a first. Like my first moustache. Barely visible.",
                "Proud of the whole group! You'd all get a seat at the back of the bus.",
                "Look who's a dungeon hero! I was a corridor hero. Held the door for everyone.",
                "A first-time clear! I'll mark it in my old school diary in red pen.",
                "Well done, brave soul. My soul was brave until I met the school nurse's needle.",
                "Outstanding. That's the kind of story I'd tell at the bike rack. With improvements.",
                "So pleased! It reminds me of the day 9B got a new football. Pure joy.",
                "You beat the boss! I beat the school chess champion. He was nine. Still counts.",
                "Up and out like a champion. Like me from the swimming pool. Gasping.",
                "Bravo, bravo! You'd have been voted best on the class trip. I voted for myself.",
                "Hah, you showed it who's boss. I showed the school bully. From a distance.",
                "This deserves a framed photo. I've got one of my cup team. I'm in front.",
                "Good work in the gloom. I worked in the gloom of the darkroom in photo club.",
                "Nice clear! I'll whistle the school song in your honour. Out of tune.",
                "Courageous! More courage than I had opening my report card in ninth.",
                "You and your friends did it. Like 9B and the great school fair raffle. We won a lamp.",
                "Fantastic! Next time, bring a cassette. Fighting music helps. Trust me.",
                "What a feeling, eh? Like scoring the winner in the school cup. I'd know.",
                "Mind your head on the way out. I hit mine on the gym doorframe every week.",
                "Tell me everything. Then I'll tell you about the school cup. It's longer.",
                "Spiders, I bet. The school cellar was full of them. I named them all.",
                "Even the teachers would clap for that. They clapped for me once. Politely.",
                "Not bad for a first go. My first go at the vaulting horse was less tidy.",
                "Into the dark you went, and came back grinning. 9B would approve.",
                "Gold star for the whole group. I keep a sheet of them for occasions like this.",
                "Was it scary? Nothing's scarier than reading your poem aloud in 8B.",
                "Back in daylight! I always squinted coming out of the school basement too.",
                "I'd have brought my bike lamp. It lit up the whole school path. Almost.",
                "Every corner checked? I checked every corner of the school for my lost cap.",
                "Huge! In my day, a deed like that got you a seat at the bike rack for life.",
                "Not even sweaty, I hope. I was always sweaty after the cup matches. Glorious sweat.",
                "Who led the way? Doesn't matter. In 9B it was always me.",
                "Big cheers from me. The kind we gave the winning team at sports day.",
                "Somebody give that group a medal. I'd make one, but my metalwork days are over.",
                "Just like a class trip! Dark tunnels, odd smells, and someone always lost.",
                "Glad you're safe. I worried about you like I worried before the cup final.",
                "Now rest your feet. I rested mine on the radiator after every winter match.",
                "Was there a map? The class trip map was upside down. I noticed. Eventually.",
                "Excellent outing. Nearly as good as the trip to the swimming baths in eighth.",
                "Mud and glory, I'd guess. Same as every football match in 1976.",
                "My goodness, you're brave. I was that brave in the school play. In cardboard armour.",
                "On your first try, too! It took me four to get my moped started that winter.",
                "Did you shout for help? Real legends don't. I shouted once. Quietly.",
                "Best news all week. Better than chips for school dinner.",
                "You've got pluck. I had pluck. Wore shorts to school in January.",
                "Out with the loot and the stories! Bring them to the bike rack.",
                "I salute your whole crew. 9B had a crew too. We met by the bins.",
                "Grinning ear to ear here. Like after my first header that went in.",
                "Monster after monster? Sounds like parents' evening in 9B.",
                "Brave one, you. I was a brave little moped rider.",
                "You and the gang survived. Like 9B survived the cabbage soup at camp school.",
                "Not one wipe? I wiped out on the ice by the school gate every winter.",
                "Treasure and triumph. In 9B, triumph was finding a coin in the snow.",
            },
