                "Lovely first kill. Like the first goal of the season. Sweetest of all.",
                "Well done, team. I'd let every one of you lean on the bike rack with me.",
                "Congrats! That beast must have been as big as our school's new gym.",
                "What a shout! I bet they heard it at the rival school. They heard mine.",
                "Down with the boss! Like 9B's chant at the cup. Down with Nordbygda!",
                "Raid victory! My best victory was beating 10C at rounders. Barefoot.",
                "Bless you all. You'd have made our cup team unbeatable. We nearly were.",
                "Hooray! I'll put on my cup final shirt and do a lap of the garden.",
                "Big win, big story. I'll tell it with me as the hero, as usual.",
                "That's what friends are for. 9B was there for me when I sprained my ankle.",
                "You beat the big bad. I beat the big bad of 9A at tag. Once.",
                "A proper clash! The cup final of 1977 was one too. We wore white.",
                "Lovely news. I'll write it in my old school diary, in capitals.",
                "Unstoppable, the lot of you. I was unstoppable on the left wing. Then the bell rang.",
                "I knew you could do it. I told everyone at the bike rack.",
                "Congrats on the scalp. In 9B we'd have hung the boss's hat on the trophy shelf.",
                "That boss was no match for you. Like the teachers' team wasn't for 9B.",
                "Fearless! Fearless like me in the school cup penalty shoot-out. Scored, too.",
                "A grand day out. Grander than the 9B trip to the cheese factory.",
                "Excellent raid! The kind of teamwork that wins school cups. I'd know.",
                "Bravo, everyone! Even I couldn't have done it alone. Probably.",
                "So pleased for you. My knees cheered too. They creaked, anyway.",
                "That boss is done for. Like the old school ball after my free kick.",
                "Mighty work, raiders! You've the strength of 9B pushing the school bus.",
                "Gosh, a first boss kill. I remember 9B's first league win. We cried. I didn't. Much.",
                "The whole group, one goal. Like 9B in the cup. The goal was mine, of course.",
                "Big, scary and beaten. Like the maths final in ninth. Well, nearly beaten.",
                "What a gang! You'd have filled the whole back of the school bus.",
                "Down in one go! I scored in one go too. Then celebrated for twenty minutes.",
                "Congratulations! I'll tell the girl in 9A. She'll be impressed. She's seventy now.",
                "Well done, all. I organised 9B's victory party. Fizzy drinks and a cassette.",
                "That's legend stuff. Ask me, I've been a legend since the cup of '77.",
                "Your raid is brilliant. Brilliant as the floodlights at the cup final. Both of them.",
                "Bravo! A kill like that makes a group into a team. I made 9B a team. Personally.",
                "A victory shout! I've got one too. You'll hear it from here. AAAH!",
                "Hearty congrats. You lot sound like 9B on the bus home from the cup.",
                "That's a big trophy. Bigger than the cup we won. Ours was a bit small.",
                "You held your nerve. I held mine in the cup final. Just about.",
                "Fantastic! The boss must feel like the rival school's goalie after I'd finished.",
                "Congrats on the triumph! Triumph is a word I learned in 9B. Used it daily.",
                "Ha! You lot would have won the school tug-of-war in seconds.",
                "Well, that's one big beast fewer. Like when the school sold the grumpy goat.",
                "Bravo! A raid that works together is like a good left wing. Fast and glorious.",
                "Mega! That's what we said in 9B. Mega. Still say it.",
                "Lovely! Every great team needs a great win. 9B had one. I scored it.",
                "That boss is toast. Like the bread in home ec. Very toasted.",
                "Big day for you. I had a day like that in 1977. I'm still living on it.",
                "Champions! I'd let you hold my cup medal. Gently. It's very old.",
                "Congrats! You've joined the big kids now. Like when I moved to the top floor in ninth.",
                "Victory feels good, doesn't it? I've felt it since 9B. Hasn't worn off.",
                "The giant fell. Like my big brother when I tripped him at Christmas. Accidentally.",
                "Splendid raid! Raids are like school discos. Big crowds, loud noise, legends made.",
                "A big boss down! I'd give the whole raid a ride on my moped. One at a time.",
                "How marvellous! In 9B a win like that got you out of homework for a week.",
                "You must be proud. I was proud in 9B. Still am. Slightly louder now.",
                "That's a gold medal kill. Like my gold at sports day. Painted cardboard, but gold.",
                "Congrats on beating it! Even the caretaker would put down his broom for that.",
                "What a roar! I roared like that when I got my moped licence. Neighbours complained.",
                "So much teamwork. Like 9B and the great school garden project. I watered.",
                "Felled at last! It took us a whole season to beat 9A at football. Then we did it again.",
                "A true raid triumph. I'd play the school song, but nobody remembers it. Except me.",
                "Massive! As massive as the queue for the school fair tombola.",
                "Ha, it's down! Like 9A's spirits after we beat them in the cup.",
                "What heroes. I'd tell 9B about you, but they've all heard my stories already.",
                "Proud of the whole raid. Like the gym teacher was proud of the whole team. And me most.",
                "Congrats! That boss must be the size of the school gym. With a beard.",
                "What a feat of teamwork. Like the class trip's human pyramid. I was on top.",
                "Lovely kill. Nearly as lovely as my goal against the teachers. Top corner.",
                "Brilliant! You'd have got a standing ovation at the school assembly.",
                "A first kill, how grand. Grand like the school cup bus. Velvet seats.",
                "Champions all! I'd have kept the ball as a souvenir. I kept mine.",
                "That's the biggest thing you've beaten. Mine was the 9B record for sit-ups.",
                "Down and done. Like 9B's season in 1978. Glorious, then over.",
                "Raid boss defeated! In my day we called that a clean sheet. And a party.",
                "Congrats, mighty raiders. Mighty like my sprint finish in the 60 metres.",
                "Wonderful! I'll dust off my old cup scarf for this.",
                "Your team's a good one. Better than 9B, maybe. Don't tell them.",
                "Bravo, all of you. I'll tell the bike rack legends. They'll nod wisely.",
                "That beast didn't stand a chance. Like my homework against the summer holidays.",
                "Big hugs to the raid. Well, firm handshakes. I'm old-fashioned.",
                "Glorious first kill! Like the first snow on the school pitch. Perfect.",
                "I'm so proud I could hum the cup final song. It went da-da-da.",
                "You're the talk of the bike rack. I made sure of it.",
                "Well done! A win like that deserves a big plate of school fair waffles.",
                "Hurrah! That boss went down like the school fence in the storm.",
                "Proud moment for the group. Like 9B lifting the cup. Mostly I lifted it.",
                "Respect, raid! That's the biggest group win since 9B's school fair stall.",
                "Victory! I celebrated mine with a cartwheel in 1977. Tore my trousers.",
                "Congrats on the kill. You'd make a fine cup team. I'd coach. And play.",
                "Down it goes, and the legend grows. Like mine did in 9B.",
                "Splendid! The rival school will hear of this. They always hear of things.",
                "How about that! Took the school three years to beat Nordbygda. You did it in a night.",
                "Bravo, bravo! I'd let the whole raid sign my cup photo. In pencil.",
                "That's a grand victory. Grand like the gym on cup final night. Packed.",
                "Ooh, a giant felled. In 9B we felled a snowman twice our size. Proud day.",
                "Congratulations! That's like winning the cup and the disco on the same day.",
                "Fine work! You'd have been the first names on the 9B team sheet. After mine.",
                "That's a win to tell. I've told mine so often it keeps getting better.",
                "You've all earned a rest. Like 9B after the cross-country. We lay on the grass for hours.",
                "Big boss, gone. Like my hair from 1977. Gone, but legendary.",
                "Lovely stuff, raiders. I raise my school milk to every one of you.",
                "Big news! I'll announce it over the school tannoy. If they let me in.",
                "A first boss kill, eh? That's like winning your first school cup match. Unforgettable.",
                "What teamwork! I haven't seen passing like that since my cup final cross.",
                "Congrats! I'd give each of you a gold star. I've been saving them since 9B.",
                "Bravo! You make an old left winger very happy.",
                "Tell me who tanked. In 9B, I tanked the whole cup final. In goal, by accident.",
                "Every healer deserves a medal. Our school nurse got none, and she earned it.",
                "Now that's a scoreboard I'd frame. Next to the 9B cup result.",
                "It took a village, eh? It took all of 9B to push my moped up the hill.",
                "Nordbygda school never beat us in a crowd. Neither did that boss beat you lot.",
                "Shoulder to shoulder, like the 9B wall for free kicks. I always ducked.",
                "Somebody tell the school paper. Front page, big letters, my name somewhere.",
                "Forty friends and one victory. Like the whole school at the last-day picnic.",
                "Was the floor shaking? It shook when 9B stamped in the gym stands.",
                "Even my old gym teacher would crack a smile. That never happened to me.",
                "Never mind the loot, feel the glory. That's what I said after the cup.",
                "Sweaty palms, I bet. Mine were sweaty before every penalty. Still scored.",
                "Hip hip hooray! That's three cheers from the self-appointed captain of 9B.",
                "Just like a cup final. Long build-up, loud finish, me shouting the loudest.",
                "Proper raid. Proper cheer. Proper legends. I know the type.",
                "Somewhere a bard is writing a song. In 9B, I wrote my own. On cassette.",
                "Was it a long fight? The 1977 cup final went to extra time. I didn't tire.",
                "Biggest win of the week, I'd say. Bigger than chips at school dinner.",
                "Tremendous. If the boss had a school, it'd be in mourning now.",
                "My, you're a mighty bunch. Mightier than 9B on a sugar high.",
                "I wish I'd been there. I'd have yelled tactics from the side, like at every match.",
                "Strategy and grit! 9B had grit. Strategy was kick it to me.",
                "Gather round, everyone. That's how I started every story at the bike rack.",
                "Well led and well followed. 9B always followed me. To the kiosk, anyway.",
                "Oh, I'd have loved to see its face. Like the rival keeper's when my shot went in.",
                "Bring the raid round for waffles. Like the school fair, but with more armour.",
                "Not bad for a bunch of friends. 9B was a bunch of friends too. And me, the star.",
                "Hard-fought and fair. That's how the school cup should be won. As I did.",
                "Into the history books! Mine's the 9B yearbook. Page one.",
                "Brave, loud and victorious. That was the motto of 9B. I made it up.",
                "So many of you, one big win. Like the whole year cheering me at sports day.",
                "One for the scrapbook. My scrapbook is mostly cup clippings. All about me.",
                "Ah, the sound of a big win. It sounds like the final whistle in 1977.",
                "Keep that feeling. I've kept mine since 9B. It fits better than my denim jacket.",
                "Somebody fetch a cup! Any cup. In 9B we drank squash from the trophy.",
                "Even 9A would clap for that, and they never clapped for anyone.",
            },
            congrats_mount = {
                "Congrats on the mount! I felt that way about my first bike. Red, with a bell.",
                "Your first mount! Park it at the bike rack with the legends. Room next to mine.",
                "A mount at last! Now you can ride past the girls of 9A like I did. Mind the kerb.",
                "Look at you, riding high. I rode high on my moped in 1977. Helmet too big, heart too.",
                "No more walking! I walked to school until eighth. Then came the bike. Life changed.",
                "Lovely! My first ride had a banana seat and a mind of its own.",
                "Congrats! I'd race you to the kiosk, but my moped's been parked since 1979.",
                "A mount of your own. Freedom, eh? I felt it the first time I biked to the lake.",
                "Well done! The moped gang would have let you join. They let me. After a year.",
                "Saddle up, legend! I saddled up on a borrowed pony at camp school. It ate my hat.",
                "Nice ride! Not as nice as my chrome handlebars, but nice.",
                "Ooh, wheels! Well, legs. I had wheels. Three gears and a dynamo lamp.",
                "Brilliant. Now you'll never be late for class again. I was. Every day. On my bike.",
                "Proud of you! My first bike made me so proud I slept next to it. Mother objected.",
                "Off you go! Wind in your hair, like me down the school hill in 1976.",
                "That's a fine mount. Fine as my moped with the tassels on the handlebars.",
                "First mount! Ride it proud. I rode my bike proudly into a hedge once. Still proud.",
                "You'll never walk again. Well, you will, but you won't want to. Trust me.",
                "Fancy! I'd give you my bike bell as a gift, but I still ring it on Sundays.",
                "A mount! The bike rack at school was where legends stood. Now you're one.",
                "Ride on! I rode my moped in my denim jacket. Looked like a rock star. Felt like one too.",
                "Lovely beast! My bike was a beast too. Rusty, but a beast.",
                "Congrats on the new ride. I put playing cards in my spokes. Sounded like a racing car.",
                "Look at you go! Faster than me on the 60 metres. Well, nearly.",
                "At last, a mount! I saved my paper round money for two years for my moped.",
                "Giddy up! That's what I shouted on my bike. People stared. I liked it.",
                "That mount suits you. Like my moped suited me. Loud and handsome.",
                "Brilliant! Ride it to the school disco. That's what I'd do. Park right by the door.",
                "Your own mount! Mine was my cousin's old bike. Squeaky, but mine.",
                "Congrats! You'll get the best spot at the bike rack now. I fought years for mine.",
                "Hooray! Mind the potholes. I hit one on my moped in eighth. Flew like a bird.",
                "First mount, eh? My first was a tricycle. Then glory. Then a moped.",
                "A noble steed! Mine was a noble moped. It coughed, but nobly.",
                "Look at that mount! The lads at the bike rack would have whistled.",
                "Well done! The first ride is the best. I still dream of my first ride without stabilisers.",
                "Up you hop! I hopped on my moped every morning. Except when it didn't start. Often.",
                "Congrats! Time to polish it every Sunday. That's what I did with my moped.",
                "Proper transport! In 9B, a bike meant status. A moped meant legend.",
                "Smashing ride! You'll be the envy of the schoolyard. I was, briefly.",
                "Saddle and all! My bike had a saddlebag. I kept my football in it.",
                "A mount, how grand. Grand like my moped licence. Framed, of course.",
                "Ride safe! I didn't, but I was fourteen and invincible.",
                "Congrats on the wheels. Or hooves. Or whatever. I had wheels. Chrome ones.",
                "Now you can carry someone to the disco. I carried Bente from 9A on my crossbar once.",
                "That's freedom right there. Freedom smells like moped petrol. Ask me.",
                "Wonderful! My first bike was second-hand. My first glory was all mine.",
                "Bravo! The school bus will miss you. I didn't miss it. Back seat was nice, though.",
                "A new mount! Give it a name. I named my moped after myself. Obviously.",
                "Ah, the first mount. Like the first time I rode no-hands. Terrifying, then legendary.",
                "Lovely ride. Ring the bell twice for me. That's what we did passing 9A.",
                "Congrats! You've graduated from walking. I graduated in 1975. With honours.",
                "You're mobile now! I was mobile on my moped. Very mobile. Too mobile, said the police.",
                "That mount is lovely. I'd let you park it by my moped. Not too close.",
                "Faster than a school bus! My moped was faster too. Downhill. With a tailwind.",
                "Well, aren't you posh. The poshest thing I rode was the headmaster's bike. Once. Shh.",
                "Hats off to your first mount. Like my first bike, it'll stay in your heart.",
                "Congrats! Now you just need a denim jacket and a cassette player. Then you're me.",
                "Up and away! I rode away from detention once. Fastest I ever pedalled.",
                "Brilliant beast! Mine had a wobbly back wheel. Gave it character.",
                "So proud! You remind me of me on my first day at the bike rack. Nervous and cool.",
                "The roads are yours now, like the school hill was mine.",
                "Lovely! I washed my moped every Saturday. Then rode it through puddles. Every Saturday.",
                "Congrats on the ride. Mine had a basket. I don't talk about the basket.",
                "At last you ride! Riding is like dancing. I was good at both. Well, one.",
                "Ride with pride. I rode with pride and a dented mudguard.",
                "Good on you. My moped had a sticker of a lightning bolt. Made it faster. Probably.",
                "A mount! That's like getting a moped licence at fifteen. Best day ever.",
                "Off on adventures! I biked to the next village once. Felt like the edge of the world.",
                "Congrats! Pop a wheelie for me. I did one in 1976. Then I did a hospital visit.",
                "Smashing! You'll never need a lift again. I needed many. My moped broke a lot.",
                "Nice mount! I'd honk my moped horn for you, but it only squeaks now.",
                "That's a proud moment. Like me rolling into school on a brand-new bike. Everyone looked.",
                "Welcome to the riders' club. Members: you, me, and the moped gang of 1977.",
                "Bravo! You've moved up to wheels. I mean, hooves. You know what I mean.",
                "Congrats! Ride to the kiosk and buy yourself a fizzy drink. That's tradition.",
                "Saddle up and smile. I smiled on my bike so much my cheeks hurt.",
                "Splendid ride! It'll get you places. My moped got me to the cup final. And nearly home.",
                "A first mount, how special. Like my first pair of football boots. I wore them to bed.",
                "Lovely creature! My bike was a creature too. It bit my trousers. Every time.",
                "Congrats! You've earned it. I earned my bike by mowing lawns. Badly.",
                "Ride on, friend! Ride like I rode on the left wing. Fast and fearless.",
                "Wheels or hooves, a ride is a ride. Mine had wheels and a leaking tyre.",
                "Bravo! Now you'll get to the disco on time. I never did. Hair took ages.",
                "That's a beauty. My moped was a beauty too. Orange. With a dent.",
                "Congrats! You'd have been the coolest kid at the bike rack. Second coolest. After me.",
                "Look at you, mounted and mighty. I was mighty on my moped. Mighty slow uphill.",
                "Hooray! I'll ring my old bike bell for you. Ding ding!",
                "Your own mount! I had to share my bike with my brother. He got Tuesdays.",
                "A mount at last! The bike shed at school smelled of rust and dreams. Lovely.",
                "Riding in style! My style was a scarf flapping in the wind. And a sore bottom.",
                "Brilliant! Go show it off. I showed off my moped every recess. Every single one.",
                "Congrats on your first mount. A day to remember. I remember mine. Rainy. Glorious.",
                "Nice! Now you can give your friends a lift. I gave Tom-Erik one. He's still scared.",
                "A grand steed. I'd trade my moped for it. No, I wouldn't. But nearly.",
                "Splendid! No more muddy boots on the way to school. I had them till ninth.",
                "Congrats! You're now officially cooler than walking. Like me in 1977.",
                "Proper wheels! Well, legs. Whatever it is, it's lovely. Mine was a rusty three-speed.",
                "Up in the saddle! I learned to ride in one afternoon. Fell off nine times.",
                "Ah, a mount. The school bus seat finally gets a rest. Mine never did. I was heavy.",
                "Congrats! You've got the look of a moped gang leader now. I had that look.",
                "Lovely mount! Don't let anyone borrow it. I lent my bike once. Never saw the bell again.",
                "Ride to glory! I rode to glory once. Well, to the corner shop. Same feeling.",
                "That's a cracking ride. Better than my bike after the hedge incident.",
                "Congrats! You've heard about my moped twice already. Here's the third time.",
                "Bravo! The first ride is like the first slow dance. Wobbly, but wonderful.",
                "A mount! You'll go far. Further than my moped. It reached the shop and back.",
                "Lovely! You're on four legs now. I was on two wheels and one prayer.",
                "Congrats on the mount. Remember to wave at the walkers. I always did. Smugly.",
                "A ride of your own! I'd have given anything for one at twelve. Got one at thirteen.",
                "Bravo, rider! You'd lead the 9B bike parade. I led it in 1976.",
                "Look at you on that thing. Like me on my moped. Proud and slightly wobbly.",
                "Congratulations! You'll never be picked last again. Mounts change everything.",
                "So nice. My first bike had streamers on the handles. Very fast streamers.",
                "Freedom and fame, that's what a mount brings. Fame came with my moped.",
                "Bravo! Ride past the bike rack slowly. Let them look. That's my advice.",
                "Congrats! A mount like that would get you a slow dance at the disco. Guaranteed.",
                "Nice wheels, er, legs. I'm still thinking about my moped, sorry.",
                "Ride it well. I rode my bike well. Through the school flowerbed, once.",
                "Congrats on the mount! I'd fix you a bike bell for it if I knew how to fit one.",
                "Up you go! Now the world's your schoolyard. Mine was the school hill.",
                "Lovely! You'll be off on adventures now. Like my bike trip to the lake. Legendary.",
                "Brilliant! I remember my moped's first start. It roared. Then it stalled. Then it roared.",
                "Hooray, a mount! I'll do a lap of the garden on my old bike. Slowly. Very slowly.",
                "That's lovely. Like the first warm day when the bikes came out at school.",
                "Congrats! Hold on tight. I didn't, once. Learned a lot about gravel.",
                "A steed for a hero. My steed was a moped. My heroism was mostly talk.",
                "Wonderful mount. My first bike's still in the shed. Rusty, but I visit.",
                "Bravo! You're too cool for the bus now. I was too cool for the bus at fourteen.",
                "Congrats! Ride it to the cup final. That's what the legends do. Did. I did.",
                "Smashing mount! Takes me back to my first moped ride. Smoke, noise, glory.",
                "I'll wave from my porch. I'm on my old bike in spirit.",
                "That's grand! Mine had stabilisers until I was nine. Don't tell anyone.",
                "Congrats! Now the long way home is the fun way home. Took me years to learn that.",
                "Mind the gravel on corners. I learned that on the school hill. Twice.",
                "Whoa there! That's what I said to my moped. It never listened.",
                "Gallop past the walkers and give them a nod. Very important.",
                "I hear hooves! Or is that my old moped coughing in the shed?",
                "Riding season has begun! In 9B it began the day the snow melted.",
                "Oh, it's lovely. Mine was second-hand and squeaked. I loved it more.",
                "Treat it well. I oiled my bike chain every Friday. Smelled of glory.",
                "Your feet can retire now. Mine retired in 1976, the day I got the bike.",
                "Off to see the world! My world was the road between home and the kiosk.",
                "Splendid steed! Give it an apple. I gave my moped petrol. Same love.",
                "Speedy! I was speedy too. Left wing, then moped. Never slowed down.",
                "Is it fast? Mine did forty downhill. Felt like a hundred.",
                "Hold the reins like I held my handlebars. Firm, but cool.",
                "That's a ride for a legend. I know legends. I see one every morning.",
                "I'm proud of you. Proud as the day I first parked at the big kids' bike rack.",
                "Ah, no more sore feet. Sore bottom, maybe. That's riding.",
                "Climb aboard, hero! I climbed aboard my moped like a knight. A small knight.",
                "Excellent mount. The girl in 9A would have asked for a ride. I hope.",
                "Proper wheels at last. Or legs. I'm old, they blur together.",
                "Hop on and wave! I waved from my bike so much I fell off. Worth it.",
                "So shiny! My moped shone like that. For one day. Then it rained.",
                "Lucky you. I had to walk uphill both ways until eighth grade.",
                "Ride it to school! Oh, you don't go to school. Ride it anyway.",
                "What a beauty! It'd turn heads at the bike rack. Mine did. Mostly with noise.",
                "Nicely done! You'll get everywhere twice as fast. I got to the disco early once.",
                "A mount like that wants a name. I'd suggest mine. It's legendary.",
                "You've joined the riders. I joined in 1976. Badge and all.",
                "Oh, I'm jealous. My first ride had a flat tyre the first day.",
                "Gosh, look at that! It's like seeing my first moped all over again.",
                "Ride proud and wave at the old folks. Like me.",
                "Pedal power is over for you. I pedalled until my moped came along.",
                "Hold on to that feeling. I've held on to mine since 1976.",
                "Faster than the bus, cooler than the bus. Like my bike was.",
                "Grand! A mount gets you places. My bike got me to the cup final. Late.",
                "Happy trails! Mine went from home to school and the kiosk in between.",
                "I'd lend you my bike clips, but they're vintage now.",
                "Beautiful ride. I can almost smell the two-stroke. Ah, memories.",
                "Travel in style! My style was flared trousers caught in the chain.",
                "Good choice. My first choice was a red bike. Then a red moped. Pattern.",
                "Hooves! I had hooves once. Wooden ones, in the school nativity play.",
                "Freedom at last. The first time I biked home alone, I took the long way.",
                "You'll love it. I loved my moped more than maths. Not hard, mind.",
                "Lovely creature. Mine had a bell, a basket and a temper.",
                "Bravo, you've got your own transport. I relied on mine till it relied on me.",
                "That's your ticket to adventure. Mine was a moped and a packed lunch.",
                "Look how tall you sit! I sat tall on my moped. On a cushion.",
                "Bless it, what a mount. I still remember my bike's squeak. A happy squeak.",
                "A ride! The school walk was forty minutes. Then my bike made it ten.",
                "Well, look at you! I looked like that the day I got my moped licence. Glowing.",
                "Now everyone will want a ride. Say no. I said yes once. Never again.",
                "Steady on, speedster. My moped topped out at thirty. I called it fast.",
                "That calls for a victory lap. Round the bike rack, like I did.",
                "How lovely. I still keep my old bike bell in a drawer. For luck.",
                "A mount and a smile. That's all a legend needs. And a denim jacket.",
                "Tally-ho! I shouted that on my bike too. People moved out of the way.",
                "Gorgeous! Mine was orange. Orange was very modern in 1977.",
                "I can hear it from here. Or that's my knees again. Congrats anyway!",
                "Brilliant! First mounts are like first loves. Mine was a bike. Then Bente.",
                "Wonderful. I'll tell the moped gang. They're all grandads now.",
                "Fair play! Earned, not given. I earned my bike with a paper round.",
                "Look out, world! Here you come. Like me down the school hill. Brakes optional.",
                "Ride it gently at first. I didn't. The hedge forgave me eventually.",
                "Officially too grand for the school bus now. Like I was.",
                "Hurray! Saddle sore tomorrow, proud forever. That's the deal.",
                "Your mount looks keen. Mine looked keen too. Then it rained.",
                "Bravo! Mind it doesn't throw you. My bike threw me into a ditch in 1975.",
                "That's a happy day. Like the day I got a new tyre for my birthday.",
                "I bet you grinned. I grinned so wide on my moped I caught a fly.",
                "On your way, rider! The open road was mine at fourteen. Well, the village road.",
                "Oh, smashing. I had a bike with a speedometer. It lied. Kindly.",
                "Well ridden already! You've got the knack. I had it too. Till the gravel.",
                "What a lovely mount. I'd draw it on my pencil case, like I did my moped.",
                "So happy for you. I've not been so happy since my moped passed its test.",
                "Bravo! You've done what I did at fourteen. Left the walkers behind.",
                "That mount's got spirit. Like my bike. It went where it wanted.",
                "Finally riding! The best summer of my life was the summer of my first moped.",
                "Very smart. My moped had a mirror. I checked my hair in it constantly.",
                "Ride on! And if anyone laughs, tell them about my moped. That'll stop them.",
                "A first mount! That's a story for the grandchildren. Mine involve a moped.",
                "Lovely, lovely. My first bike was a gift from Granny. Pink. I rode it proudly.",
                "Now you're sorted. I was sorted at fifteen. Moped, jacket, cassette.",
                "Keep it clean. I polished my bike's chrome till I could see my fringe.",
                "You'll never be late again. I was late on my moped too. It was the hair.",
                "Best feeling in the world, that. Second only to scoring in the school cup.",
                "Your first ride! Mine was a hand-me-down with a wonky seat. Treasured it.",
                "Bravo! I'd salute you with my moped helmet, but it's a flowerpot now.",
                "Steady as she goes! That's what Granddad said when I first rode. I didn't listen.",
                "A mount, at last. The longest wait of my life was for my moped licence.",
                "You must be beaming. I beamed so much on my first bike that I hit a fence.",
                "That's a well-earned ride. I earned mine by washing cars. Badly.",
                "Saddle up, champ. Champions ride. I rode, so I must have been one.",
                "Ooh, does it have a bell? Every ride needs a bell. Mine went brring.",
                "Bravo! You can visit me now. I'm just past the school, by the old bike rack.",
                "Congratulations, rider! Your first ride is the one you'll never forget.",
                "Off into the sunset! I rode into the sunset once. Then had to ride back for tea.",
                "A fine mount. My moped had a seat for two. It was usually just me.",
                "Ha, look at you! Like me on my moped. Except you look like you know what you're doing.",
                "Ride hard! Or gently. My knees prefer gently these days.",
                "You got there! I remember saving every coin for my bike. Every single coin.",
                "A first mount! That's like your first school disco. Unforgettable. Bit wobbly.",
                "In my day, a bike made you king of recess. A moped made you emperor.",
                "Lovely mount! It'll be your best friend. My moped was mine. Until Bente.",
                "Bravo! Ride with your chin up, like the legends at the bike rack.",
                "I'm so pleased. My first bike changed everything. My second changed nothing.",
                "Hooray! Now go fast, but not too fast. Learned that the hard way in eighth.",
                "Mount acquired! I acquired my moped the summer of 1976. Best summer.",
                "Look at that saddle! My bike saddle was hard as a school bench.",
                "What joy. The first ride home is the best. I took the long way past 9A's houses.",
                "Proper rider now. I was a proper rider. Mostly in my own head.",
                "Bravo, friend. May your mount be faster than my moped. Low bar.",
                "Off you trot. I trotted to school for years. Then I flew. On a bike.",
                "It's a big day. I had a big day like this when the bike shop opened in our village.",
                "A mount! Freedom comes on four legs. Mine came on two wheels. Close enough.",
                "Lovely. I'll put on a cassette and imagine I'm riding with you.",
                "Bravo! My moped's horn played a tune. Just the one tune. All summer.",
                "Ride with style, like a 1977 legend. Collar up, of course.",
                "Congratulations on your new companion. Mine was a moped called Lightning.",
                "Well, aren't you mobile! I was mobile until my chain came off. Then I walked.",
                "Good stuff! You'll find the shortcuts. I knew every shortcut to the kiosk.",
                "What a day! The day I got my bike, I rode till dark. Then past dark.",
                "So exciting! I couldn't sleep the night before my moped came.",
                "My moped had a sticker that said Turbo. It wasn't. Yours looks faster.",
                "Bravo! Riding's in your blood now. It's been in mine since my first bike.",
                "Lovely mount. Bet it doesn't need pushing uphill. Mine did. Often.",
                "A real treat. Like the day I got a dynamo light. Saw the road for once.",
                "You're on your way now. Literally. I was on my way at fourteen. Still going.",
                "Bravo, rider! I can see you galloping. I galloped too, on the school field. On foot.",
                "What a thrill. Like the first time the moped started on the first kick. Rare thrill.",
                "Excellent! You'll get to every party first. I got to every party first. Then left last.",
                "Your own ride! No more asking for lifts. I asked Dad for years. He sighed a lot.",
                "Good luck out there. Watch for puddles. They got me every spring.",
                "A lovely first mount. You'll remember it like I remember my red bike.",
                "Bravo! Now teach it some tricks. My moped knew one trick. Stalling.",
                "Riding high, eh? I rode high once. Tall bike, short legs. Tricky.",
                "Well done! I'm putting a gold star next to your name. Right below mine.",
                "Lovely! My bike had a reflector. I thought it made me a racing driver. No.",
                "Fabulous! I bet you'll ride it everywhere. I rode my bike to the toilet once. Indoors.",
                "Ride with care, ride with flair. That was the motto of the moped gang.",
                "My first proper ride was the school's old tandem. With Tom-Erik. Chaos.",
                "Off you go then! Don't forget to come back for tea. I always forgot.",
                "Great mount! It's like having a moped and a friend at once. Lucky you.",
                "That's the dream! I dreamed of a moped every night in eighth. Then it came.",
                "Bravo! You've left the walking club. I left it with a bang. Literally.",
                "Lovely news! I'll ride my old bike to the shop in your honour. Slowly.",
                "Look at you, all grown up and riding. Reminds me of 9B. Everyone had a bike but Roger.",
                "A trusty steed! Mine was trusty. Except on Mondays. And in rain.",
                "Nice! Next stop, the bike rack of fame. I'll save you a spot.",
                "Brings a tear to my eye. My first bike did too. Mostly the wind.",
                "Kick-start it with confidence. That's how I did my moped. Then I pushed it.",
                "Remember me when you ride past the bike rack. Legends deserve a wave.",
                "Trot, canter, gallop. I only knew pedal, wobble, fall.",
                "Never mind the bus fare now. I spent mine on sweets at the kiosk.",
                "Chrome or fur, it's all glory. Mine was chrome and rust.",
                "Just think of the places you'll go. I went to the lake. Twice a week.",
                "Go on, show it to everyone. I showed my moped to the whole of 9B.",
                "Our village had one moped in 1976. Mine. Now yours is the famous one.",
                "Hear that? It's freedom. Sounded like a two-stroke engine in my day.",
                "Every legend needs a ride. Mine was a moped with one working light.",
                "Your mount is grand. Mine was grand too, apart from the brakes.",
                "Did you do a little lap? I did ten laps of the yard on day one.",
                "Be kind to it. My bike and I had our arguments, but we made up.",
                "Swapped your boots for a saddle! I swapped mine in 1976. Best trade ever.",
                "First mount, eh? My granny cried when I got my moped. Fear, mostly.",
                "Shine it, ride it, love it. My three moped rules, 1977.",
                "Clip clop! I made that noise on my bike for a whole summer.",
                "My heart races just looking at it. Like the cup final. Or the stairs.",
                "Enjoy the breeze. Best thing about my moped was the wind in my fringe.",
            },
            congrats_epicmount = {
                "An epic mount! That's like going from a bike to a moped. I remember the day.",
                "Congrats on the fast one! I tuned my moped once. It went faster. Then it went bang.",
                "Now that's speed. Faster than me on the 60 metres in eighth. Almost.",
                "Look at you, upgraded! Like when I swapped my bike bell for a moped horn.",
                "Epic indeed. The tenth-graders had a motorbike like that. We all stared.",
                "Brilliant! The moped gang leader had something that fast. I was second in command.",
                "Zoom! That's the sound I made on the left wing. Now it's the sound you make.",
                "A fast mount at last. The girls of 9A would only see a blur. Like they saw me.",
                "Proud of you! It took me two summers of paper rounds to afford my moped upgrade.",
                "The big league now. Like going from 9B to the cup final team. I did that.",
                "Swift as the wind! I was swift once. Ask the defenders of 1977.",
                "Well, aren't you grand now. Grander than the headmaster's car. And that had leather seats.",
                "An epic ride! I'd race you, but my moped only reached jogging speed.",
                "Bravo! Now you can outrun anything. I outran the caretaker once. Glorious day.",
                "Faster than the school bus, the teachers and the bell. That's the dream.",
                "Congrats on the speed! My fringe would never have survived that wind.",
                "That's a legend's mount. I was voted a legend at the bike rack. By me.",
                "Oh my, the speed! I went that fast once. Downhill, no brakes, 1976.",
                "Lovely! The older boys had mopeds that fast. They let me sit on one. Once.",
                "Epic! That word wasn't used in 9B. We said smashing. This is smashing.",
                "You've moved up to the fast lane. I lived in the fast lane in 1977. Moped, 30 km/h.",
                "Congratulations! You'll be at the kiosk before the bell even rings.",
                "A proper steed now. Mine was a proper moped. With a proper rattle.",
                "Look at that beast! In 9B we'd have crowded round it at recess.",
                "Faster, stronger, prouder. That's how I felt on my moped's first full tank.",
                "Brilliant upgrade. Like trading my old football for the leather one. Never looked back.",
                "Bravo! An epic mount for an epic friend. I'm epic too, by the way. Since 1976.",
                "So fast! You'll leave everyone in the dust. I left Roger from 8C in the dust. Often.",
                "Pure class. Class like my denim jacket with the patches. Very classy.",
                "Hold on tight! I didn't, on the 1976 downhill. The ditch remembers.",
                "A fast one! I'll tell the lads at the bike rack. They'll be green with envy.",
                "Congrats! You must feel like the fastest kid in school. I was that kid. Briefly.",
                "Epic mount, epic grin. I had that grin when I scored in the school cup.",
                "Splendid! Even the moped gang would step aside for you. They never did for me.",
                "Wow! My moped did thirty with a tailwind. You've got me beat.",
                "You've earned the fast lane. I earned mine on the school sports day. Gold.",
                "What a machine! Er, creature. I'm stuck on mopeds, forgive me.",
                "Bravo! Speed suits you. It suited me too. On the left wing.",
                "A grand upgrade. Like going from the bench to the starting eleven. I did that once.",
                "That mount is glorious. I'd give my cup medal for a ride. No, I wouldn't. Nearly.",
                "Congrats on the epic! It'll get you to the disco before the slow dances. Smart.",
                "Speedy friend! You'll be home before the school bus leaves. I always was. On foot.",
                "That's the top shelf. The top shelf at the kiosk had the best sweets. Now you're there.",
                "Wonderful! My moped had flames painted on it. You've got real speed. Lucky.",
                "Epic mount! That's the cup final of mounts. I know about cup finals.",
                "Proud of you. Proud like the day I got a moped with gears. Three of them!",
